summary:
  frontDoor offers a directory row's address on a private host for an
  audition.

history:
  The catalogue is publicly writable and nobody clicked. A row naming
  192.168.1.1 would send the player knocking on the listener's router, and on
  the uuid road the address could be saved.

target:
  package/contents/ui/HealLogic.js

find:
          return host !== "" && !HostGuard.isPrivateHost(host) ? t : "";

replace:
          return host !== "" ? t : "";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_heallogic.qml::test_a_door_into_the_listeners_own_network_is_no_door.
  Line-neutral.
